#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid "Creating a new signature"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To create a new signature, go to <menuchoice> <shortcut> <keycombo action="
"\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>N</keycap></keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>File</"
"guimenu> <guimenuitem>New</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>. This will create an "
"<guilabel>&lt;empty signature&gt;</guilabel> in the <guilabel>Signatures</"
"guilabel> section. <mousebutton>Left</mousebutton> click the &lt;empty "
"signature&gt; and in the bottom section type in your new signature. "
"<example> <title>Signature example</title> <screen>\n"
"Mr. Konqi\n"
"konqi@kde.org\n"
"http://www.kde.org\n"
"</screen> </example> Once you have completed your signature, save it by "
"going to <menuchoice> <shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>S</"
"keycap></keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Save</"
"guimenuitem> </menuchoice>, or by pressing the <guibutton>Save</guibutton> "
"button (floppy disc icon)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to use the same first or last lines of text in your signatures "
"use the menu items <guimenuitem>Edit Standard Header</guimenuitem> or "
"<guimenuitem>Edit Standard Footer</guimenuitem> from the <guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can create as many signatures as you would like. Doing so provides you "
"with a list of signatures to use in email applications such as &kmail;, so "
"no matter how informal or professional you need to be, there will always be "
"an available signature."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid "Deleting a signature"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To remove a signature first select the signature that you want to remove and "
"then click <menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Remove</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>, or by clicking the <guibutton>Remove</guibutton> "
"button with the red x icon in the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:152
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adding signatures to &kmail;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adding signatures is pretty straight forward."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Open &kmail; and go to <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure KMail...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> In the "
"<guilabel>Identities</guilabel> page, highlight the identity to add the "
"signature to and then press the <guibutton>Modify...</guibutton> button on "
"the right-hand side of the window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the <guilabel>Signature</guilabel> tab. Check the <guilabel>Enable "
"signature</guilabel> box. From the <guilabel>Obtain signature text from</"
"guilabel> drop down, select <guimenuitem>Output of Command</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now you have the choice to enter two different command in the "
"<guilabel>Specify command</guilabel> text box to add the signatures you "
"created with &ksig;:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>ksig --daily</command>: Use the same random signature for one day."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>ksig --random</command>: Use random signatures for each mail."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:171
#, no-c-format
msgid "and then press the <guibutton>OK</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

